subject: Add microG trusted vault backend

Provide a TrustedVault backend so sync encryption works without Play Services.

The backend is implemented against the microG "Folsom" key retrieval
service: fetchKeys performs the GMS broker handshake (service id 172,
SECURITY_DOMAIN "chromesync") and returns the shared keys held by microG,
createKeyRetrievalIntent delegates to the service's UX flow, and
markLocalKeysAsStale is forwarded as well. Operations that would write to
the security domain (recovery methods, opt-in) stay disabled.

This replaces the previous stub backend, whose fetchKeys always returned
an empty key list and therefore made password sync fail with a
cryptographer error, and drops the SyncSettingsUtils change that
suppressed the sync error in settings: with a working backend the error
state can be reported honestly again.

Note: no GMS class is taken from the Play services basement jar. An
earlier version of this patch depended on
google_play_services_basement_java for ApiMetadata and Status, but the
build failed at dex time: R8 reported ApiMetadata as defined multiple
times, once in the basement jar and once in this target's javac jar.
The GMS types this backend needs (ApiMetadata, Status, ConnectionInfo)
are therefore vendored here under
org.chromium.components.trusted_vault.gms, next to the broker handshake
types (GetServiceRequest, IGmsCallbacks, IGmsServiceBroker) that already
lived there for the same reason: the basement jar already ships them,
R8 rejects the duplicate classes at dex time, and the real ones cannot
be used (no public constructor or setters on GetServiceRequest, no Stub
on IGmsCallbacks, no asInterface on the broker Stub). The Folsom types
(SharedKey and the AIDL interfaces) stay in their real
com.google.android.gms.auth.folsom packages: nothing in the app depends
on the auth-base jar, so they cannot collide, and the Parcel round-trip
carries their class names. Only the Java package changed for the
vendored types; the wire protocol (descriptors, transaction numbers,
field numbers) is untouched.
